# Mosquitto ACL for the TLS listener (8883) -- see IMPROVEMENTS.md finding A3.
# Only `app` (the phone) and `bridge` (bridge_esp32) authenticate here; the
# loopback listener (1883) stays anonymous/unrestricted for local Pi tooling
# and isn't affected by this file.
#
# The bridge only ever publishes sensor readings and per-node telemetry -- it
# never subscribes to anything (see bridge_esp32_wifi_fallback.ino, the only
# bridge variant that is an MQTT client at all; the UART bridge reaches
# Mosquitto indirectly through serial_bridge.py on the loopback listener and
# never authenticates here). Scoping it to publish-only on exactly those
# topics means a compromised/spoofed bridge can't send actuator commands,
# rewrite rules, or read anything back.
#
# /battery and /mesh are NOT optional extras: the deep-sleep telemetry work
# (2026-07-26) made the bridge publish both on every reading, and the app's
# Mesh Map screen consumes them. They were missing from this list, so
# Mosquitto silently denied every one of those publishes -- keep this list in
# sync with the firmware's publish sites or telemetry disappears with no error
# anywhere except the broker log.
user bridge
topic write greenhouse/+/air/temperature
topic write greenhouse/+/air/humidity
topic write greenhouse/+/soil/moisture
topic write greenhouse/nodes/+/status
topic write greenhouse/nodes/+/battery
topic write greenhouse/nodes/+/mesh

# The app is the trusted end-user client: dashboard, actuator control,
# weather rules, notification settings, camera, history -- needs the full
# namespace both ways.
user app
topic readwrite greenhouse/#
